Hi everyone,

Dean, I don't understand your answer. For my part, I have no problem to reach the inputs:

rm(list = ls())
library(shiny)

A <- c(1,2,3)
B <- c("A", "B", "C")

ui =fluidPage(
  numericInput("num", label = h3("Numeric input"), value = 1),

  uiOutput('essai'),
  uiOutput('essai2')

)
server = function(input, output, session) {

  output$essai <- renderUI({

    lapply(1:input$num, function(i){

      sliderInput(B[i],"text", min=0, max=A[i], value=0)

    })

  })

  output$essai2 <- renderUI({
    if(is.null(eval(parse(text = paste0("input$", B[3] ))))){}
    else{
      p(eval(parse(text = paste0("input$", B[3] ))))

    }

  })
}
runApp(list(ui = ui, server = server))

I recognize this code is not the most elegant way to do it but for me, it is running efficiently.

Dean, what do you think ? Is there another way to do it (i.e. without eval parse) ???

Cheers

