I would start by just dropping the jquery reference from your template (and if you're seeing double jqueryui references in your browser's developer tools, then try dropping jqueryui as well). If you intended to wrap up this functionality as a reusable R package, then it would be worth talking about some of the more formal ways of declaring HTML dependencies that let Shiny resolve all the various libraries that different components want to load, and do the right thing--but if this is just for a one-off project, then it's totally fine for template.html to just "know" that jquery will already be loaded.

